                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "I was drawn in by the visuals, and I can confirm that the map itself is breathtaking in VR. The track however looks a little out of place and kind of breaks the aesthetics, but it’s not a huge issue as your senses will be pretty occupied with the obstacles ahead. \n\nThanks to the power of VR you’re in for a extreme ride. The platform you’re standing on moves fast, and you have to move really quickly in all directions within your playspace in order not to smack into the walls ahead. \n\nRoomscale coaster is the game to play if want to improve your stamina and ducking abilities. It’s simply an excellent workout game that might also give you an adrenalin rush. \n\n[i]I played without the comfort option and didn’t feel any nausea, but then again I think my VR feet are pretty much fully grown by now.[/i]",
